fix(ssh): retain select values without duplicate binding warnings

Tokio 1.54.1 select expands branch bindings into both a pattern-only readiness match and the actual handler. CI force-warn unused_variables overrides the macro readiness match allowance, reporting the otherwise consumed identifiers.

Rename only the five new PTY select bindings and their real uses. Preserve branch order, biased/default polling policy, futures, exact error values, all five journey windows, and every assertion. No allow, ignore, baseline, dependency, or gate changes.

Validation: git diff --check and inverse rename byte comparison passed. No Rust toolchain is available locally, so no compile, Clippy rerun, or runtime test is claimed.
